    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d76">

                <pb facs="0220" n="128" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg128"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/7727</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-02-21T20:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 21, 1918, 8 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 8.08 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>8764. My 8748, February 20. Fürstenberg sent the following message to Czernin
                    yesterday: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>As soon as the text, which has been mutilated in several places, has been
                            definitely established I shall ask His Majesty to receive me <pb
                                facs="0221" n="129" xml:id="pg129"/> in order that I may deliver the
                            message to him tomorrow evening, February 21.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>The Austro-Hungarian Minister of Foreign Affairs has sent the following
                    supplementary message to the Ambassador at Madrid: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>If Mr. Wilson assents to the King’s proposal and sends a representative
                            to discuss matters with me he should send some one who speaks either
                            French or German as I do not know English well enough to discuss such
                            weighty matters.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Page</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
